.\" ixargs man page
.TH IXARGS 1 "" "ixargs"
.SH NAME
ixargs \- interactive xargs: run commands against stdin lines in a split-pane TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ixargs
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I cmd
[\fIargs\fR...]
.PP
.B ixargs
[\fIoptions\fR]
.B \-\-
.I cmd
[\fIargs\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ixargs
reads lines from standard input and runs a command for each line in an interactive
split-pane TUI. Select a line to run the command with that input; output appears
in the adjacent pane with scrolling and color preserved.
.PP
The first non-option argument (or the first after
.B \-\- )
is the command; remaining arguments are passed to it. Use
.B \-\-
to separate ixargs options from command arguments that look like options (e.g.
.BR find (1)
with
.BR \-exec ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-z " [" \fICOLS\fR|\fI%\fR]
Split horizontally (list on left, output on right). Optional
.I COLS
or percentage (e.g.
.B 40
or
.B 25% )
sets the list width; default is automatic.
.TP
.BR \-v " [" \fILINES\fR|\fI%\fR]
Split vertically (list on top, output below). Optional
.I LINES
or percentage (e.g.
.B 10
or
.B 25% )
sets the list height; default is 10 lines.
.TP
.B \-t
Trim leading and trailing whitespace from each input line.
.TP
.BR \-I \fI replstr\fR
Replace
.I replstr
in the command arguments with each stdin line instead of appending the line.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B j
/
.B \(da
Next line
.TP
.B k
/
.B \(ua
Previous line
.TP
.B Space
Next page
.TP
.B b
Previous page
.TP
.B <
Top of output
.TP
.B >
Bottom of output
.TP
.B q
Quit
.TP
.B ?
Help
.TP
.B /
Search (stub)
.TP
.BR n " / " N
Search next / previous
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run
.B echo
for each line:
.RS
.EX
printf 'a\enb\enc\en' | ixargs echo
.EE
.RE
.PP
Horizontal split (list left), run
.B wc \-l
on each file:
.RS
.EX
ls | ixargs -z wc -l
.EE
.RE
.PP
Vertical split (list top), run
.B head \-5
on each:
.RS
.EX
ls | ixargs -v head -5
.EE
.RE
.PP
Replace a placeholder in the arguments:
.RS
.EX
printf 'foo\enbar\en' | ixargs -I '{}' echo "file: {}"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use
.B \-\-
when the command has option-like args:
.RS
.EX
printf 'foo\enbar\en' | ixargs -I '%' -- find . -exec grep % {} \e;
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xargs (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at: https://github.com/acbeers/ixargs/issues
